<title>TURKEY: Turk Arcelik Q1 profits jump 144.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Arcelik Q1 profits jump 144.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   428.51 vs     263.15</p>
<p>    Net profit		  2,892.43 vs   1,184.19</p>
<p>    Net sales		  28,653.59 vs  16,072.07</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  6,293.97 vs   3,037.15</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  741.63 vs     264.41</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense     1,305.56 vs     902.96</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1,854.20 vs     874.96</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense     108.17 vs	44.40</p>
<p>    Total debts		34,199.17 vs  20,604.80</p>
<p>    Equity		     23,499.50 vs  11,236.05</p>
<p>    Capital		     6,750.00 vs   4,500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading durables producer Arcelik A.S. is largely owned by leading industrial conglomerate Koc Holding.</p>
<p>The company will distribute a 300 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal share from its 1996 profits from May 30.</p>
<p>It plans to raise capital to 10,125 billion lira by issuing 3,375 billion lira of bonuses, or 0.5 bonus for one existing share. 1,350 billion lira of bonuses will be financed by additional dividends from 1996 profits and the rest from other company funds.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
